ion": "Japan", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 1.5, "unitsMaximum": 1.5, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["FLD"], "gradingBasis": "SUI", "gradingBasisShort": "S/U NoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Satisfactory/Unsatisfactory (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/02/2019", "sessionEndDt": "01/19/2019", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "Combines classroom sessions and international experience with an increased awareness of business environments outside the United States. On trips, students visit local businesses, subsidiaries of foreign multinationals, government officials, local business school students, and others. Students also must attend two pre-trip meetings during the semester (2-1/2 hours each). These meetings are used to present information on international business conditions, industrial structures, management styles, and also to develop cross-cultural skills. Students also must attend one post-trip meeting with a discussion and analysis of their impressions from the trip. A final paper, integrating the material learned in the classroom with their experiences, is required. Students in some treks do pro bono consulting projects for small and medium size companies. Hence, the PowerPoint is the deliverable in those cases.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(CU-ITL)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, winter, spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "Course fee: required faculty-approved study trip.", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: Johnson School students only.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2720, "crseId": 363059, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NBA", "catalogNbr": "5991", "titleShort": "Global Business Strategy", "titleLong": "Global Business Strategy", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 1065, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "01/02/2019", "endDt": "01/19/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "eai1", "firstName": "Elena", "middleName": "A.", "lastName": "Iankova"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": null, "bldgDescr": null, "facilityDescrshort": null, "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/02/2019", "endDt": "01/19/2019", "addConsent": "N", "addConsentDescr": "No Special Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "DW", "instrModeDescrshort": "DL WWW", "instrModeDescr": "Distance Learning - WWW", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": null, "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "OPT", "gradingBasisShort": "Stdnt Opt", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter or S/U grades", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "AEM", "catalogNbr": "3991", "type": "W"}], "sessionCode": "WS", "sessionBeginDt": "01/02/2019", "sessionEndDt": "01/19/2019", "sessionLong": "Winter Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": null}], "description": "In today's increasingly globalized and interconnected world, international transactions as part of business are the norm. Even purely domestic firms have to deal with international issues, be it in the form of imported supplies or foreign competitors. In addition, more and more companies are going abroad to pursue their major business objectives. How can they take advantage of the global marketplace and create economic value through their multimarket activities? This course has three integrated objectives: first, to give you a basic grounding in global business, so that you can become capable of understanding and analyzing events and trends in the global business environment and their impact on managerial decision making; second, to help you understand the analytical frameworks on strategy formulation and implementation in an international context; and third, through a series of concrete case discussions and a local product internationalization project, the course aims at developing your practical skills in applying the tools of global strategic analysis in concrete business situations. Its ultimate goal is to help you become better prepared to serve in and lead business organizations in today's globalized world.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Summer, Winter.", "catalogComments": "Co-meets with a section of AEM 4940.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2019-01-31T19:14:21-0500", "catalogDttm": "2019-01-31T19:15:35-0500"}}